ceedings of DiGRA 2023: Limits and Margins of Games"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-8720986e-026e-4550-907a-14e6b4fa0a2a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Enacted Sociality in Single-Player Play","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718881","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"This paper asks how identity may be constructed, maintained, or developed in the practise of playing, and how this can be indicated in play with single-player digital games. Namely, the goal is to decipher games’ pedagogical inclinations along with the players’ positioning in these towards learning processes which may establish a frame of identity development potential. This is done via the concept of transformative learning situations in gameplay as potentials of identity formation. This, in terms of both the sociocultural and constructivist implications of engagement with a game as culturally situated artifact, and the pedagogical view of these in relation to the practise itself. While this paper is a theoretical discussion around the single-player play-practise with single-player digital games in combination with literature on identity, it is also closely linked to the intricacies of qualitative studies on and of these phenomena. For this reason, the focal points of the discussions are centred on re-evaluating assumptions of research and methodological issues towards the cultural play-practise of identity and play. In this sense, the paper poses issues and questions towards utilizing learning theory to study games, and vice versa, while also providing questions towards assumptions in studying games and identity development through learning.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Graham, Mike Hyslop"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383277"],"event":{"acronym":"ECGBL","title":"European Conference on Games Based Learning"},"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Identity play","Learning processes","Play Practise","Single Player Games","Transformative Learning Theory"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"single player digital games hegemonical dialogical or critical agents in identity formation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86349846/GBL_094_Single_player_digital_games_Final_Copy.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383277","identifier":[{"id":"85120714530","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-8953de5b-9b0a-4ef7-84f4-60fb0591f428"],"keyword":["Identity play","Learning Processes","Play Practise","Single Player Games","Transformative Learning Theory"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-191C975BC6DEEFE5A793B090DD657C84"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86349846/GBL_094_Single_player_digital_games_Final_Copy.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Games Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mike Hyslop","key":"grahampau","last":"Graham","locid":"59264501-60c6-4666-87c2-73d7a42a4ff0","name":"Graham, Mike Hyslop","orcid":"0000-0002-3667-3253","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Panagiotis","key":"fotarispedh","last":"Fotaris","name":"Fotaris, Panagiotis","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.34190/gbl.21.094","eisbn":["9781914587139"],"isbn":["9781914587122"],"pages":"825-831","publisher":"Academic Conferences and Publishing International","status":"p","title":"ECGBL 2021- Proceedings of the 15th European Conference on Game Based Learning"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85120714530"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-8953de5b-9b0a-4ef7-84f4-60fb0591f428"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Single-Player Digital Games: Hegemonical, Dialogical, or Critical Agents in Identity Formation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383277","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
